<div class="page">
  <div>
    <h1>Polar Careers</h1>
    <h2>Email Signature Line Tips</h2>
    <p>Now that you have entered college, you have also become a young professional (college student). So, it's time to step up your professionalism by creating an appropriate email signature line for use with your ONU email address which is appropriate to use as your professional email since you get to keep it for life as long as you continue to use it. To learn how to set up your signature line in Gmail, go <a href="#">here</a>.</p>
    <p>Here are tips from <span data-field="full_name">{{ full_name }}</span> who is a small business collaborator and the founder of the <span data-field="employer.name">{{ employer.name }}</span>.</p>
    <p>Keep it as short as you can while providing all of the information you deem most important (for lines is the accepted standard).</p>
    <p>Condense information into fewer lines by using pipes ( | ) or colons (: ) to separate the text.</p>
    <p>Remember that simple plain text is best; skip special fonts and graphics.</p>
    <p>Use the accepted signature delimiter ( ~ ) to help your signature get recognized as such by email clients.</p>
    <p>Be careful with HTML formatting because it may not appear how you want it to for everyone.</p>
    <p>Test your signature with as many email clients as you can, especially if you use HTML.</p>
    <p>Avoid written out URLs instead of using hyperlinks in your email to ensure the link will go through in the sent message.</p>
    <p>Avoid including multiple phone numbers and email addresses. Pick your contact preference and get rid of the rest.</p>
    <p>Skip your mailing address — not every recipient wants or should have to access that information.</p>
    <p>Include links to your most important social media profiles, only if they are appropriate.</p>
    <p>Include your email address. You can't rely on various email clients to include header information in replies and forwards.</p>
    <p>Consider different versions, both in length and content and know when to use each version (i.e. use a shorter version on replies).</p>
    <p>Make sure you update your signature on your mobile device if you frequently use it to send messages. Here are some quick how-to's on popular devices:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><span data-field="skills[0]">{{ skills[0] }}</span></li>
      <li><span data-field="skills[1]">{{ skills[1] }}</span></li>
    </ul>
    <p>Reconsider including a quote; you never know when you might offend someone or give the wrong impression.</p>
    <p>Avoid including a legal disclaimer unless required to do so.</p>
    <p>Avoid including a virus-checked message at the bottom of every email.</p>

    <div class="signature-block">
      <h2>EXAMPLES OF EFFECTIVE PLAIN TEXT EMAIL SIGNATURES</h2>
      <div class="contact-info">
        <p><strong>Default version:</strong></p>
        <p>Name: <span data-field="full_name">{{ full_name }}</span></p>
        <p>Major | Grad Date | Ohio Northern University</p>
        <p>Phone: <span data-field="phone_number">{{ phone_number }}</span> | Email: <span data-field="email_address">{{ email_address }}</span> | Website: <span data-field="website_url">{{ website_url }}</span></p>
        <p>Twitter: <span data-field="social_media_handle_twitter">{{ social_media_handle_twitter }}</span> | LinkedIn: <span data-field="social_media_handle_linkedin">{{ social_media_handle_linkedin }}</span></p>
      </div>
      <div class="contact-info" style="margin-top: 20px;">
        <p><strong>Replies:</strong></p>
        <p>Name: <span data-field="full_name">{{ full_name }}</span></p>
        <p>Phone: <span data-field="phone_number">{{ phone_number }}</span></p>
        <p>Website: <span data-field="website_url">{{ website_url }}</span></p>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top: 25px; font-size: 10pt;">#POLARPARDISE #SKILLSFORLIFE #WEGOTTHIS #PolarCareersRocks #OrangeDoor2ndFloor</p>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Polar Careers, <span data-field="employer.department">{{ employer.department }}</span> | Division of Academic Affairs</p>
      <p style="font-size: 10pt;">PHONE: <span data-field="phone_number_contact">{{ phone_number_contact }}</span> | EMAIL: <span data-field="email_address_contact">{{ email_address_contact }}</span> | WEB: <span data-field="website_url_contact">{{ website_url_contact }}</span></p>
      <div class="social-icons" style="margin-top: 15px;">
        <img src="placeholder_facebook.png" alt="Facebook">
        <img src="placeholder_instagram.png" alt="Instagram">
        <img src="placeholder_youtube.png" alt="YouTube">
        <img src="placeholder_linkedin.png" alt="LinkedIn">
        <img src="placeholder_twitter.png" alt="Twitter">
      </div>
    </div>
